{
  "name": "libreDSSP",
  "description": "An open-source interpreter for DSSP (Dialog System for Structured Programming), a Soviet stack-based language originally developed for the Setun ternary computer. The implementation provides a modular execution environment with support for core dictionary words, user-defined functions, and multi-stack management in a C-based runtime. It features integrated GNU Readline support for an interactive REPL and maintains high fidelity to the original language's concatenative programming philosophy.",
